      "math_academy_id": "q-225067",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(4)$ given below, compute $P(3\\le X<6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0916\\,$ | $\\,0.2381\\,$ | $\\,0.4335\\,$ | $\\,0.6288\\,$ | $\\,0.7851\\,$ | $\\,0.8893\\,$ | $\\,0.9489\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X<6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(3\\le X<6) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(3\\le X<6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X<6) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.7851-0.2381 \\\\  & =0.5470.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
